### Register a new merchant - success
POST http://localhost:8080/merchants/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "soban{{$uuid}}@example.com",
  "password": "SecurePass123!"
}

### Register - missing email (expect 400)
POST http://localhost:8080/merchants/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "password": "SecurePass123!"
}

### Register - invalid email format (expect 400)
POST http://localhost:8080/merchants/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "password": "SecurePass123!"
}

### Register - password too short (expect 400)
POST http://localhost:8080/merchants/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "shortpass{{$uuid}}@example.com",
  "password": "abc"
}

### Register - duplicate email (run the "success" request above first with a FIXED email, then repeat this exact request twice)
POST http://localhost:8080/merchants/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "duplicate-test@example.com",
  "password": "SecurePass123!"
}

### ^ Run the request above TWICE in a row - second call should return 409 EmailAlreadyRegistered


### Login - success (use the fixed email/password you just registered above)
POST http://localhost:8080/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "duplicate-test@example.com",
  "password": "SecurePass123!"
}

### Login - wrong password (expect 401, generic message)
POST http://localhost:8080/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "duplicate-test@example.com",
  "password": "WrongPassword!"
}

### Login - nonexistent email (expect 401, SAME generic message as wrong password)
POST http://localhost:8080/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "doesnotexist@example.com",
  "password": "SecurePass123!"
}

### Login - missing password field (expect 400, @NotNull on LoginRequestDTO)
POST http://localhost:8080/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "duplicate-test@example.com"
}